# Top-level packages installed into the isolated runner image. The per-arch
# .lock files are the digest-pinned dependency closure of this list; regenerate
# them with gen-lock.sh after any change here. cli/toolcatalog.go declares which
# binary each entry provides, and TestCatalogPackagesAreDeclared asserts the two
# agree.

# base: shell-free execution, scratch handling, and the guard firewall
bash
binutils
file
iptables
libcap-utils
openssl
python3

# foothold carrier: the ssh client an operator-declared foothold uses to carry
# commands to a host the operator already controls. It is deliberately absent
# from the tool catalog, so it is not a reachable command and the model cannot
# invoke it; only the code-built carrier in cli/foothold.go runs it.
openssh-client

# network and DNS reconnaissance
bind-tools
curl
masscan
nmap
nmap-ncat
tcpdump

# service enumeration
net-snmp-tools
nbtscan
nfs-utils
openldap-clients
samba-client
sslscan

# web and content discovery
# dnsrecon is deliberately absent: Alpine's package imports the stamina module,
# which has no Alpine package, so the tool fails at startup. DNS enumeration
# uses bind-tools (dig, host, nslookup) instead.
ffuf
jq

# identity and directory
krb5

# cloud and cluster
aws-cli
kubectl

# exploitation and analysis
gdb
john
py3-impacket
socat
